### ADR-003: Hosting & Edge Runtime — Cloudflare Pages

**Status**: Accepted
**Date**: [YYYY-MM-DD]

#### Context
Need hosting with:
- Global edge network (low latency)
- Zero-config deployments from Git
- Support for TanStack Start (Vite + SSR)
- Free tier for development
- Custom domains, SSL, headers

#### Decision
Deploy to **Cloudflare Pages** with **Cloudflare Workers** for edge functions.

#### Consequences
**Positive**:
- True edge runtime (V8 isolates, not Node.js) — cold start ~0ms
- Generous free tier (500k requests/month, unlimited sites)
- Git integration (auto-deploy on push)
- Built-in D1, KV, R2, Queues for future expansion
- WAF, DDoS, bot protection included
- `wrangler` CLI for local dev (`wrangler pages dev`)

**Negative**:
- **No Node.js APIs** — must use Web Standards (Fetch, Streams, Crypto)
- No `fs`, `path`, `process` — polyfills needed for some packages
- 10ms CPU limit per request (free), 30ms (paid)
- 128MB memory limit
- No long-running processes (use Queues/Durable Objects)

**Neutral**:
- TanStack Start Cloudflare adapter handles most incompatibilities
- Supabase JS client works (uses Fetch)

#### Alternatives Considered
| Alternative | Pros | Cons | Why Not Chosen |
|-------------|------|------|----------------|
| Vercel | Best Next.js support, edge functions | Cost at scale, vendor lock-in, no free tier for teams | Cost predictability |
| Netlify | Good free tier, edge functions | Less performant edge, fewer primitives | Cloudflare network superior |
| AWS Amplify + Lambda@Edge | Enterprise features | Complex, expensive, slow deployments | DX |
| Fly.io / Railway | Full control, containers | More ops, not edge-native | Team size |

#### Implementation Notes
- `wrangler.toml` config for Pages + Functions
- `output: 'server'` in TanStack Start config (SSR)
- Edge-compatible dependencies only — audit with `wrangler pages dev`
- Use `@cloudflare/kv-asset-handler` for static assets if needed
- Custom domain via Cloudflare Registrar or CNAME
- Preview deployments on every PR

#### Validation Criteria
- [ ] `wrangler pages dev` matches production behavior
- [ ] All npm dependencies resolve without Node.js polyfills
- [ ] Cold start < 100ms (measured via Workers Trace)
- [ ] Deploy preview URL works for every PR

